/* RP2350A (Adafruit Feather RP2350, 8 MB QSPI flash) memory map. Verified against
   embassy-rp-0.10.0 build.rs and rp-pac-7.0.0 (same verification hil/pico-seplos-emu/memory.x
   records — mirrored here verbatim). RP2350 replaces the BOOT2 second-stage bootloader (RP2040)
   with an IMAGE_DEF block (auto-generated by embassy-rp's lib.rs macro for feature "_rp235x",
   placed in the `.start_block` linker section by the PAC).

   WP1 (delight-features, 2026-07-25): board moved from a Pico 2 (4 MB flash) to an Adafruit
   Feather RP2350 (8 MB flash) — same silicon, wider flash window. FLASH LENGTH below re-derived
   for 8 MB; RAM is UNCHANGED (flash was never this target's constraint; RAM was — see
   `../s/src/mem_layout.rs`'s header comment for the RP2350's actual 520 KiB contiguous SRAM vs.
   the 512 KiB this split still conservatively claims).

   Stage 4 (EPIC #350, story S4 #355) TrustZone-M S/NS split: this crate is now the NS-WORLD HALF
   of the split — the `s` crate (secure world) owns the first 128 KiB of flash and first 64 KiB of
   RAM (see `../s/memory.x` / `../s/src/mem_layout.rs`, the split's single Rust-side source of
   truth). Origins/lengths below shifted per that split's derivation (reported to this crate's
   territory in `s/memory.x`'s comment, applied here):
     FLASH ORIGIN 0x10000000 -> 0x10020000 (past the S image + its 4 KiB NSC veneer subregion),
       LENGTH 8M -> 0x7E0000 (8064 KiB) so the NS region still ends at the Feather's 8 MB flash
       window (0x10000000 + 8M = 0x10800000 = 0x10020000 + 0x7E0000).
     RAM ORIGIN 0x20000000 -> 0x20010000 (past the S image's 64 KiB), LENGTH 512K -> 0x70000
       (448 KiB) so the NS region still ends at the 512 KiB SRAM boundary this split claims
       (0x20000000 + 512K = 0x20080000 = 0x20010000 + 0x70000) — NOT the chip's full 520 KiB (the
       last 8 KiB, 0x20080000-0x20081FFF, is available headroom this work package deliberately
       leaves unclaimed; see `s/src/mem_layout.rs` for why).
   Both new origins are 4 KiB-aligned (far coarser than the 32-byte SAU/MPU minimum granularity),
   matching the SAU regions `s/src/sau.rs` programs for `NS_FLASH_BASE`/`NS_RAM_BASE`. */
MEMORY {
    FLASH : ORIGIN = 0x10020000, LENGTH = 0x7E0000
    RAM   : ORIGIN = 0x20010000, LENGTH = 0x70000
}

/* For RP2350, place the IMAGE_DEF block (.start_block) between the vector table and .text,
   within the first 4 KB of THIS image's own FLASH region (relative to the new NS FLASH origin
   above, not the chip's absolute 0x10000000). Under the Stage 4 S/NS split, the boot ROM no
   longer scans this NS image directly (it boots the `s` image at the chip's real
   0x10000000 origin, which `bxns`-jumps here via `s/src/ns_jump.rs` reading this image's raw
   vector-table words, not any IMAGE_DEF metadata) — embassy-rp's "_rp235x" feature still
   auto-generates this `.start_block` section unconditionally, so it still needs a placement or
   the link fails on an orphan section; kept for that reason, not because the boot ROM reads it
   here anymore.
   After .start_block, recalculate _stext to account for the block's size. */
SECTIONS {
    .start_block (ADDR(.vector_table) + SIZEOF(.vector_table)) : ALIGN(4) {
        __start_block_addr = .;
        KEEP(*(.start_block));
        _stext_offset = .;
    } > FLASH
} INSERT BEFORE .text;

/* Override cortex-m-rt's default _stext to place .text after .start_block. */
_stext = _stext_offset;
